Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7eaa022-12cf-592a-ab07-2eeadefc2793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,2,4,8,{2,4},{2,8},{4,8},{2,4,8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395716} {:answer/id #uuid "9a08b3e3-eb17-5ee2-bea5-1b56ef752421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{2},{4},{8},{2,4},{2,8},{4,8},{2,4,8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395717} {:answer/id #uuid "f2402890-c172-5742-b423-263e71997747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{{2},{4},{8},{2,4,8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395718} {:answer/id #uuid "e2daa154-1445-566e-ae93-ed4fffaad295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{2,4,8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395719} {:answer/id #uuid "6f836ae3-47dc-5686-af54-b563d298bfd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{2},{4},{8},{2,4},{2,8},{4,8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a08b3e3-eb17-5ee2-bea5-1b56ef752421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{2},{4},{8},{2,4},{2,8},{4,8},{2,4,8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395717} :answer-field/id #uuid "595f6f8e-2567-512e-a222-db6ad6900a59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "350a2acf-787e-5ee2-949f-2438ca3d2b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-1203" :question/problem "If $X={2,4,8}$, then $P(X)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram. \n\n![](images/58/580d7c32378a2af641fb1066cec4ec24cc6c5b140ccf9475f9a3e3a68367d30d.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n∅={},\\,{2},\\,{4},\\,{8},\\,{2,4},\\,{2,8},\\,{4,8},\\,{2,4,8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)={∅,{2},{4},{8},{2,4},{2,8},{4,8},{2,4,8}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f1f99d3-ebcb-50c6-a162-bd58f7d5ec92" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b227e33-90e1-52cd-95bf-25d66f7bc6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371640} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc4222c-6364-5c17-8622-1f69d49752c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371641} {:answer/id #uuid "22ba1cfd-c6e0-5b5a-995c-5444fefa4b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{{∅},{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371642} {:answer/id #uuid "d8162a07-3d4a-590f-bc92-e15e82030d4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371643} {:answer/id #uuid "8bcac1e6-e07b-5469-9b8b-ea8057b9214c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8162a07-3d4a-590f-bc92-e15e82030d4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371643} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8af6849-bbbd-5257-abdf-809ae009ea35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7946c285-f988-5068-b516-3298112d9fdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-1204" :question/problem "If $Y={0}$, then $P(Y)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $Y,$ denoted $P(Y),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $Y,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list out the subsets of $Y:$\n\n- The subset with no elements is $∅.$\n\n- The subset with $1$ element is $Y$ itself: ${0}.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y)={∅,{0}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd097735-fa55-589d-9594-34bdbd607a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65\\,536" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372393} {:answer/id #uuid "3a46b546-0817-517d-ae23-82a6eae47732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372394} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0e2f07-9331-5d38-9395-f8fc67c1c11e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,024" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372395} {:answer/id #uuid "6921ab35-c60f-5f43-9eba-0889e5f87645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372396} {:answer/id #uuid "d28a898e-a62b-5210-bada-7d9a8db4dc32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd097735-fa55-589d-9594-34bdbd607a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65\\,536" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372393} :answer-field/id #uuid "8713ad7c-37d7-5134-a2cb-fa0ff4713712" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23139fd9-d255-51c7-b39b-28cddd3cf6e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-182215" :question/problem "If $|B|=2$ then $|P(P(P(B)))|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S$, we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $|B|=2.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n|P(B)|={2}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(B))| & ={2}^{|P(B)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{4} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(P(B)))| & ={2}^{|P(P(B))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{16} \\\\  & =65\\,536.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bafffb-5f0c-5c61-9e90-3d17123e83b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383675} {:answer/id #uuid "052967b6-fb43-5e95-a31e-43b0b94be836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383676} {:answer/id #uuid "55b8265d-0309-53c7-9240-42c3bc5039a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383677} {:answer/id #uuid "8196ea70-1091-54e2-b900-6d0e1a1e1d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383678} {:answer/id #uuid "f748cce5-3e62-5bf7-9d93-1c282e88d229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8196ea70-1091-54e2-b900-6d0e1a1e1d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383678} :answer-field/id #uuid "148bd5bb-a19e-5aa5-8d46-0156bb7a5c5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17503d54-27f5-530c-9f6d-5a30b7aa466b" :question/math-academy-id "q-182218" :question/problem "If $|X|=0$ then $|P(P(P(X)))|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S$, we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $|X|=0.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n|P(X)|={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(X)))| & ={2}^{|P(X))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(P(X))| & ={2}^{|P(P(X)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa2c4ff-0153-57ef-b2da-d7857daa6674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372407} {:answer/id #uuid "0738be5e-320c-53d1-b477-85f540ec0e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372408} {:answer/id #uuid "213da24e-3ba3-56e1-8f70-a2a77cb72023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372409} {:answer/id #uuid "66674441-1c75-53d9-86ed-276306c7f760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372410} {:answer/id #uuid "8542c241-c995-5fef-bed2-cf1e26117a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0738be5e-320c-53d1-b477-85f540ec0e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372408} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c64fa3-c4a7-55bf-986b-6474978ea29c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a57e2ec-6280-5dcd-8f47-bb36c3489753" :question/math-academy-id "q-182223" :question/problem "If $Y={1}$ and $Z={m,n}$ then $|P(Z)\\times P(Y\\times Z)|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|Y|=1,\\,|Z|=2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(Y\\times Z)| & ={2}^{|Y\\times Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|Y|\\,\\cdot \\,|Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1\\cdot 2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(Z)\\times P(Y\\times Z)| & =|P(Z)|\\cdot |P(Y\\times Z)| \\\\  & ={2}^{|Z|}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaa3babe-fc8a-5abc-bbf5-d3767d792f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453616} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e55f60-ad7a-5563-b5e2-159c439a70ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaa3babe-fc8a-5abc-bbf5-d3767d792f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453616} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7fdab7-f983-5bc2-bb04-1f895b807dfb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de45af91-7568-5e47-b37f-4413eeae542d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453618} {:answer/id #uuid "710b6a64-0fde-520e-acb4-e44ce684997e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de45af91-7568-5e47-b37f-4413eeae542d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453618} :answer-field/id #uuid "c726e020-da13-5ea6-bafe-4ed894d72a26" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1d878aa-3421-5025-86bd-8a47672bae55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453620} {:answer/id #uuid "84aca991-7429-5390-ab6f-fd636bcc8a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84aca991-7429-5390-ab6f-fd636bcc8a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453621} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd9eceba-08ff-5052-86b4-313736cb0156" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a540711c-ecf6-55f0-99c0-da5fdfa24e62" :question/math-academy-id "q-182224" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(∅)={∅,{∅}}$\n- **II.** $P({a,∅})={∅,{a},{a,∅}}$\n- **III.** $P({∅})={∅,{∅}}$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that we are given the set $∅.$ So, its power set must be ${∅}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${a,∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{a},{∅},{a,∅}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${∅}$ is ${∅,{∅}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aab99129-4a35-5556-a306-b270209eb006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471197} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf24b5c-acad-501b-ba57-b7184be25122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdf24b5c-acad-501b-ba57-b7184be25122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471198} :answer-field/id #uuid "6763cbff-5062-54e7-8246-c7e4594fed34" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef9dd66-34ea-5dbf-a0dd-8474aee33837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471199} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd0b854-f3ec-55e0-ab08-b2d4550ee97e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aef9dd66-34ea-5dbf-a0dd-8474aee33837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471199} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5e493a5-5150-5cd4-919d-2373e95ae21f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0bb31f-6825-5c25-8cf0-baac756459f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471201} {:answer/id #uuid "fd50a221-4939-518b-9637-343788a92231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f0bb31f-6825-5c25-8cf0-baac756459f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471201} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f2aeba-3fe6-5e39-aeca-5cc3601e1920" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d277777-ae06-5b12-9091-65c43e7bf489" :question/math-academy-id "q-182241" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n- **I.** $P({Z,t,n})$\n- **II.** $P(Z)$\n- **III.** $P({{2}^{n}∣n\\in Z})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,t,n})={∅,\\,{Z},\\,{t},\\,{n},\\,{Z,t},{Z,n},\\,{t,n},\\,{Z,t,n}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $8.$\n\n- Set II is infinite since the underlying set $Z$ is infinite.\n\n- Set III is infinite since the underlying set ${{2}^{n}∣n\\in Z}$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8778d1d6-56f8-53d0-84ba-767e63081689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471203} {:answer/id #uuid "2537b203-09cf-557c-81b0-c475fc88df1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2537b203-09cf-557c-81b0-c475fc88df1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471204} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9fd90d-669d-50c1-802c-52fd43a9167d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90dd7fd-1407-5087-9054-8b8b023a110b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471205} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff656d2-5368-5e0a-8da4-07c3a6941a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d90dd7fd-1407-5087-9054-8b8b023a110b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471205} :answer-field/id #uuid "231ab226-6dc0-5f17-aa30-afeaf13ed198" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac414c0f-0d3d-5718-8e84-dee85e47be80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471207} {:answer/id #uuid "2d40b22a-54ca-5e3a-974f-5f328d7636a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d40b22a-54ca-5e3a-974f-5f328d7636a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471208} :answer-field/id #uuid "8478d074-7469-5128-92b8-f86d4edc7c75" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c6c0e2c1-4d3b-51cf-9630-3617d7834c7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-182242" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $P(P(∅))={∅,{∅}}$\n- **II.** $P(P({∅}))={∅,{∅}}$\n- **III.** $P(P({0}))={∅,{∅},{{0}},{∅,{0}}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the power set of the set $∅$ is ${∅}.$ Therefore, $P(P(∅))={∅,{∅}}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{∅}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({∅}))={∅,{∅},{{∅}},{∅,{∅}}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that we are given the set ${0}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{0}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({0}))={∅,{∅},{{0}},{∅,{0}}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a45469e-136a-5e5b-b99c-d0986cc05aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471209} {:answer/id #uuid "34298241-b946-5a36-9d6f-cdccc915da9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a45469e-136a-5e5b-b99c-d0986cc05aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471209} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5ec5c4-62cb-56d9-bab7-8189327c57a5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472110} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bc87f60-846a-5297-91f2-4b0d573ccaf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471211} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2c37cf-9e89-5f2f-836e-fe89e922b1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2c37cf-9e89-5f2f-836e-fe89e922b1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471212} :answer-field/id #uuid "7348f3ad-5c47-51b6-adc0-96ac7ad27556" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e69bd74-d6db-5f41-aaba-1646f9178cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471213} {:answer/id #uuid "c008f84e-6f4f-5a9b-bf98-a8afad9a4478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e69bd74-d6db-5f41-aaba-1646f9178cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471213} :answer-field/id #uuid "68fd73fa-c23e-5720-9d17-1ef1a6a7e99e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "afe01a46-709c-5c6f-b721-547dd77ac300" :question/math-academy-id "q-182244" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $P(P(2))={∅,{2}}$\n- **II.** $P(P({2}))={∅,{∅},{{2}},{∅,{2}}}$\n- **III.** $P(P({{2}}))={∅,{{2}}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that $2$ is not a set. So, the notation $P(P(2))$ does not make sense.\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that we are given the set ${2}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{2}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({2}))={∅,{∅},{{2}},{∅,{2}}}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that we are given the set ${{2}}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{{2}}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({{2}}))={∅,{∅},{{{2}}},{∅,{{2}}}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f1f99d3-ebcb-50c6-a162-bd58f7d5ec92" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db71e7bd-17a7-5c3e-b85a-d855980fc5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{{1}},{{2}},{1,2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380134} {:answer/id #uuid "9afd1ad0-ae36-5146-84d8-5c44ef606ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{{1},{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380135} {:answer/id #uuid "31ae5193-c036-5292-9647-0a6694c97596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{1},{2},{{1},{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380136} {:answer/id #uuid "23878966-27c7-561d-87e1-4baea08b0446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{1},{{2}},{{1},2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380137} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9f45c3-c995-5225-aa34-1fbb010aea0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{{1}},{{2}},{{1},{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e9f45c3-c995-5225-aa34-1fbb010aea0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∅,{{1}},{{2}},{{1},{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380138} :answer-field/id #uuid "540f0f32-e64b-559d-8803-d14a4f38339f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5de41a0c-cbd2-54e7-9d6b-cea2337e1df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-80959" :question/problem "If $B={{1},{2}},$ then $P(B)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $B,$ denoted $P(B),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $B,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $B$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](images/10/1043ca38333d8e62100931c1676cba3dc85521134b60b4a5682142618c447cbd.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $B$ are\n\n$$\n∅={},\\,{{1}},\\,{{2}},\\,{{1},{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\nP(B)={∅,{{1}},{{2}},{{1},{2}}}.\n$$"}]}
